---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import MinutesForm from '../components/MinutesForm.astro';
import { books, CATEGORIES, countIn, plural } from '../lib/books.js';
import { SITE } from '../site.config.js';

const jsonld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Organization',
  name: 'Book and Gin Society',
  alternateName: 'BAGS',
  url: SITE.url,
  description:
    'A book club in Wellington, New Zealand, that meets monthly, usually at Southward Distillery in Lyall Bay. There is no set book: members bring what they have been reading and discuss it.',
  foundingDate: '2025-02',
  address: { '@type': 'PostalAddress', addressLocality: 'Wellington', addressCountry: 'NZ' },
};
---
<Base
  title="Book and Gin Society: A Book Club That Meets at a Gin Distillery"
  description="A monthly book club with no set book. Members bring what they've been reading, and every book we discuss goes on the shelf."
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonld)} />

  <section class="hero">
    <p class="label" style="color: var(--grey)">The Book and Gin Society, est. {SITE.founded}</p>
    <h1>A book and gin society where, somewhat to everyone's surprise, we actually talk about <span class="serif-em">the books.</span></h1>
    <div class="hero__foot">
      <p class="hero__sub">On the last Friday of every month we meet, usually at Southward Distillery in Lyall Bay, open with a toast, and talk about whatever we've been reading. This is where the books end up.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/shelf">Browse the shelf</a>
        <a class="link-plain" href="#minutes">Send me the minutes</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>Convenes</dt><dd>Last Friday, monthly</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Usually at</dt><dd>Southward Distillery, Lyall Bay</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Set book</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
    <div><dt>On the shelf</dt><dd>{plural(books.length, 'book', 'books')}</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <section class="section split" aria-labelledby="what-title">
    <h2 id="what-title" class="label">What this is</h2>
    <div class="prose-lg">
      <p>The Book and Gin Society has met since February 2025, under a charter we take about as seriously as you'd expect. There's no set book and no homework. Each of us brings whatever we've been reading, Soft or Hard, Fiction or not, and tells the room what it did to us.</p>
      <p>Some of us read a hundred books a year, and some of us are mainly here for the gin. Somehow the conversation always comes back to the books.</p>
      <p class="muted">The gin is optional, the non-alcoholic options are poured with equal ceremony, and dogs are welcome. Membership is by invitation and meetings are in person only, so you can't join us on a Friday. You can, however, see everything we've talked about.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush-top" aria-labelledby="shelf-title">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="shelf-title" class="label">The Shelf</h2>
      <a href="/shelf">Browse the shelf</a>
    </div>
    <ol class="benefits">
      <li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><p>Each book is listed with the member who brought it. Every book here was worth talking about, even the ones someone wishes they'd never read.</p></li>
      <li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><p>Every book is filed as Soft or Hard, Fiction or Non-Fiction. Most of us live somewhere between Soft and Hard Fiction, and a select few prefer Hard Non-Fiction, so you'll always know which shelf your people are on.</p></li>
      <li><span class="n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><p>Books brought as warnings are marked as such, and those are well worth reading about.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="tiles">
      {CATEGORIES.map((c) => {
        const [first, ...rest] = c.name.split(' ');
        const dark = c.slug === 'hard-non-fiction';
        return (
          <a class:list={['tile', { 'tile--dark': dark }]} href={`/shelf/${c.slug}`}>
            <span class="tile__name">{first}<br />{rest.join(' ')}</span>
            <span class="tile__count">{plural(countIn(c.slug), 'book', 'books')}{dark && ', a select few'}</span>
          </a>
        );
      })}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="minutes" class="minutes minutes--full" aria-labelledby="home-minutes-title">
    <div class="minutes__copy">
      <p class="label">The Minutes</p>
      <h2 id="home-minutes-title">The Minutes.</h2>
      <p>After every meeting, a short note goes out listing every book we discussed. It's the next best thing to being there, and considerably cheaper.</p>
    </div>
    <div aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <MinutesForm id="home-minutes-email" />
  </section>

  <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-title">
    <div class="chapter__text">
      <h2 id="chapter-title">Start your own chapter.</h2>
      <p>A kit for founding your own society is coming soon.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="pill">Coming soon</span>
  </section>
</Base>
